# Frame by Frame architecture

- `src/lib/types.ts` is types only. `src/lib/schema.ts` is Zod. `progress.ts`, `week.ts`, `search.ts`, and `webgl-guard.ts` stay pure.
- `src/hooks/` binds React to `src/lib/`. Do not put business rules in a hook.
- `src/content/` is typed curriculum data. No logic. Every resource needs `cost` and `verified`. Every assignment needs at least two done-when checks. `npm run validate` must pass after a content edit.
- `src/routes/` is one file per route, composition only. `src/components/ui/` is shadcn. Wire tokens; do not restyle primitives with new colors.
- Learner progress uses the single versioned localStorage key behind `useProgress`. Do not add a server for that state.
- Every static route is prerendered at build (`src/entry-server.tsx` → `dist-ssr/`, `scripts/prerender.ts` → `dist/<path>/index.html`, `404.html`) from the same `routes` in `src/router.tsx`. A new static route goes into `PRERENDER_ROUTES`, `routeModule()` and `e2e/expected-headings.ts`. `main.tsx` hydrates only via `shouldHydrate` (`src/lib/hydrate-guard.ts`).
- **No browser reads during render.** `window`, `document`, `localStorage`, `matchMedia`, `navigator` and `new Date()`-dependent output may be read in effects, event handlers, or behind `useHydrated()` (false in the prerender and the hydration render). Per-user state renders a neutral server snapshot (progress `{ blank, "empty" }`, never `"unavailable"`; theme `"system"`; media queries `false`) and switches after hydration. Layout that depends on the viewport is CSS (`display: none` on the inactive variant), never a render-time media query.
- Post-hydration state loads that change context run in `startTransition`, and context values stay memoized, so a route boundary still hydrating is never forced to client-render. Client-only chrome (cookie banner, toaster, Lenis, sticky CTA) stays behind the deferred `LaunchChrome` import.
- After a change that touches rendering, run `npm run build && npm run e2e:preview` (zero `[hydration]` errors across routes, themes, stored state, phone and desktop).
- Path alias `@/*` maps to `src/*`. Tests live next to the code as `*.test.ts` or `*.test.tsx`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — a route computes week clamping itself
const week = Math.min(16, Math.max(1, Number(n)));

// ✅ GOOD — the route reads a pure helper
const week = parseWeekParam(n);
```
